<p>Sumi leads the comparable-budget group on knowledge, coding, and reasoning. But the commonsense results tell a different story: Sumi scores 66.4 on PIQA and 60.0 on HellaSwag, well behind Llama 2-7B's 78.7 and 76.2. The likely culprit is Sumi's <em>education-heavy</em> data mixture — filtering for educational content improves reasoning benchmarks but hurts the casual-web-text patterns that commonsense tasks rely on.</p>

<table class="results-table">
  <thead><tr><th>Task (commonsense)</th><th>Sumi-7B</th><th>Llama 2-7B</th><th>OLMo-7B</th></tr></thead>
